WEBVTT

00:00.450 --> 00:03.687
Alright crew, this is Part 1: know the system.

00:03.637 --> 00:09.227
Before you climb anything, you need to know how our lights get their power, and why we wire them the way we do.

00:10.183 --> 00:12.308
Six rules to live by.

00:12.258 --> 00:14.018
Power off first.

00:14.018 --> 00:16.055
Fifty lights on a circuit.

00:16.055 --> 00:18.821
Fill to eighty percent, never the top.

00:18.821 --> 00:21.136
One wire, one breaker.

00:21.136 --> 00:23.925
Cut the positive wire at every injection.

00:23.925 --> 00:26.576
And test on Pure White before you leave.

00:27.543 --> 00:29.472
Think of a garden hose.

00:29.422 --> 00:31.111
Volts are the push.

00:31.111 --> 00:32.778
Amps are the flow.

00:32.778 --> 00:34.919
Volts don't start fires.

00:34.919 --> 00:36.366
Amps do.

00:36.366 --> 00:39.167
Our light wire is thin, twenty gauge.

00:39.167 --> 00:40.973
That's the thin hose.

00:40.973 --> 00:43.739
Push too much flow through it and it gets hot.

00:43.739 --> 00:45.764
So we keep the flow small.

00:46.727 --> 00:48.876
That's what Class 2 is about.

00:48.826 --> 00:52.541
Each circuit only carries a little power, about four amps.

00:52.541 --> 00:54.647
And we never fill to the top.

00:54.647 --> 00:57.969
A six hundred watt box, you use four hundred and eighty.

00:57.969 --> 01:01.395
A four amp breaker, you use three point two amps.

01:01.395 --> 01:05.423
Plan fifty lights a circuit and five circuits a box, and you're covered.

01:05.423 --> 01:08.235
Never put in a bigger breaker to stop trips.

01:09.199 --> 01:11.672
Here's how the power box is wired.

01:11.622 --> 01:16.124
Wall power comes in from a GFCI outdoor plug at a hundred and twenty volts.

01:16.124 --> 01:18.844
The supply turns it into twenty-four volts.

01:18.844 --> 01:23.011
The board splits that into six circuits, each with its own four amp breaker.

01:23.011 --> 01:25.337
The controller sends the colour data.

01:25.337 --> 01:27.883
Feeders carry power out to the lights.

01:27.883 --> 01:30.198
One wire, one breaker.

01:30.198 --> 01:35.869
One six hundred watt box holds about two hundred and fifty lights, around a hundred and sixty-five feet.

01:35.869 --> 01:38.207
Never more than two hundred and eighty.

01:39.159 --> 01:43.090
Mount the box near a GFCI outdoor plug, out of the rain.

01:43.040 --> 01:44.950
Four corner screws.

01:44.950 --> 01:49.568
Run the output cable in conduit, and seal every spot a wire leaves the box.

01:50.519 --> 01:52.725
Rule one, every time.

01:52.675 --> 01:55.256
Box off before you plug in any light.

01:55.256 --> 01:56.657
Then hook up.

01:57.607 --> 01:59.975
Test on the ground before you climb.

01:59.925 --> 02:04.497
Hook up fifty lights and check them in the app, on Pure White, not just colours.

02:05.463 --> 02:06.929
Here's why.

02:06.879 --> 02:10.119
The sticker says zero point nine six watts a light.

02:10.119 --> 02:13.406
On Pure White it really pulls one point three seven.

02:13.406 --> 02:15.582
That's forty-three percent more.

02:15.582 --> 02:19.321
A run can look fine on red and still trip the breaker on white.

02:19.321 --> 02:22.319
PW is the white on the far left of the app.

02:22.319 --> 02:23.963
Not BW.

02:24.911 --> 02:27.604
Power and data pass from light to light.

02:27.554 --> 02:29.648
The data goes all the way.

02:29.648 --> 02:31.095
Never cut it.

02:31.095 --> 02:35.146
Power fades the further it goes, so the far lights go dim or yellow.

02:35.146 --> 02:39.475
That's why we inject new power every fifty lights, about thirty-three feet.

02:39.475 --> 02:42.380
At every injection, cut the positive wire.

02:42.380 --> 02:43.908
Never the data.

02:44.863 --> 02:50.009
On the house, the lights click into the track on the fascia, facing out and tipped a little down.

02:49.959 --> 02:52.066
Y-connector at every corner.

02:52.066 --> 02:57.251
A signal booster before any extension over ten feet, and at every jump to the second floor.

02:57.251 --> 03:00.144
And an end cap on the last light of every run.

03:01.095 --> 03:02.595
Now the ladder.

03:02.545 --> 03:04.351
Set it four to one.

03:04.351 --> 03:06.851
One foot out for every four feet up.

03:07.823 --> 03:12.460
On pavement, bumpy ground, or in wind, your partner holds the base.

03:13.375 --> 03:16.102
Three points of contact at all times.

03:16.052 --> 03:19.085
Tools go in your belt, never in your hands.

03:19.085 --> 03:25.034
Keep your belt buckle between the rails, don't reach too far, and stay ten feet away from power lines.

03:25.983 --> 03:27.483
Quick recap.

03:27.433 --> 03:29.193
Power off first.

03:29.193 --> 03:31.091
Fifty lights a circuit.

03:31.091 --> 03:33.070
Fill to eighty percent.

03:33.070 --> 03:35.385
One wire, one breaker.

03:35.385 --> 03:37.676
Cut the positive at injections.

03:37.676 --> 03:39.505
Test on Pure White.

03:40.463 --> 03:42.033
That's Part 1.

03:41.983 --> 03:44.934
Now take the Part 1 quiz in your training portal.
